# rsync exclude list. Deploys to /home/ian/.rsync-excludes (see laptop-backup.sh EXCLUDES).
# Paths are relative to SRC (/home/ian/). Leading slash anchors to SRC root.
# Goal: back up what a wipe destroys, skip what the internet re-provides.

# --- Re-downloadable toolchains and package caches ---
/.arduino15/
/.rustup/
/.cargo/registry/
/.npm/
/.cache/
/.local/share/Trash/

# --- App payloads that reinstall themselves ---
/snap/
/.steam/
/.var/app/*/cache/

# --- Large re-fetchable downloads ---
# Cut installer images. Keep the rest of Downloads.
/Downloads/*.iso

# --- Generic caches anywhere in the tree ---
**/Cache/
**/CachedData/
**/Code Cache/
**/GPUCache/
**/.cache/

# --- Editor and OS junk ---
*.tmp
*~
.DS_Store

# --- Unreadable by the backupsrc rrsync session (added 2026-09-06) ---
# These come back "Permission denied (13)" and force rsync exit 23. None of
# them are worth restoring: browser-managed state, IPC sockets, key material.
/.ssh/
/.config/ibus/
/.var/app/*/config/ibus/
/.local/share/nano/
/.local/share/nautilus/scripts/
/.local/share/Trash/expunged/
/.config/BraveSoftware/Brave-Browser/Local State
/.config/BraveSoftware/Brave-Browser/CertificateRevocation/
/.config/BraveSoftware/Brave-Browser/PKIMetadata/
/.config/BraveSoftware/Brave-Browser/Crowd Deny/
/.config/BraveSoftware/Brave-Browser/Default/blob_storage/
# Brave component/extension version dirs: <32-char id>/<n.n.n>/
/.config/BraveSoftware/Brave-Browser/*/[0-9]*.[0-9]*/
